#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:49
#: f92f1258058a40aa9348ca8680f2ef94
msgid "Induced Noise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:51
#: 9f6f4315a67d4fa0b9bdea01ab14ff54
msgid "On large vehicles, the power or motor phase lines usually run in parallel with the signal lines which provides an opportunity for high frequency noise coupling. This can sometimes drastically impair the ESC operation as show below in this video:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:56
#: 3f091127b71a498d9804eb5b9df0702c
msgid "Here are scope traces of the above situation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:61
#: 538bd7e048d946d3ba2181eea7781a38
msgid "As the current ramps, noise is being induced into the analog signal until it finally is corrupt enough to be interpreted by the ESC as shutdown pulse width, which it does, allowing the signaling to recover and repeat the cycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:63
#: b995a904d696472da5d9da9243ba7668
msgid "Expanding the section where the shutdown occurs, you can see that the analog signal finally gets noisy enough for its digital logic level to be incorrectly interpreted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:69
#: c10de7e8bf8640bd932007c6d96526ec
msgid "Solutions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:71
#: fe1809245f3640a49995eb5f1fb26d83
msgid "Physically separate the signal wiring from the power wiring to the ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:72
#: d1c9bce195f142ba951444e214c6d141
msgid "Place a small toroidal choke (designed for the 1-10MHz range) in each ESC signal line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:73
#: c36816f2709747ba8a3e2483a19ed1b6
msgid "Add capacitor banks to power inputs of ESC. See next section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:76
#: f61a7cb1e2e84ae0aa58f6f67c871b7a
msgid "ESC Overvoltage Spikes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:78
#: 68d5900cb10e44d29e58fdc020e159ac
msgid "Long power cabling runs from the battery to the ESC on larger vehicles can produce large voltage spikes due to the lead inductance. These spikes not only increase noise, increasing the potential for noise coupling to the signal control lines of the ESC, but also can be potentially directly damaging to the ESC. This can be reduced or eliminated by adding low ESR capacitance at the ESC power inputs. An example of the typical capacitor bank for these applications is offered by `Advanced Power Drives <https://powerdrives.net/cap-bank>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:81
#: bd15b7f3355a4df7b3073154369e08e0
msgid "ESC Firmware Bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:83
#: 6072a0d23b464524859c3dbf53ed7b76
msgid "Some ESC firmware versions contain bugs which can seriously impact correct operation with ArduPilot. The following lists some known bugs which users should be aware of. Where workarounds are available they will be listed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:89
#: e7f93fbfae61471a86d76ab2eaace14d
msgid "APD ESCs with anti-spark connectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:91
#: 5b21aee83c1d4824a03dc8de59026983
msgid "Vehicles running anti-spark connectors and APD ESCs with firmware versions dated before November 2022 may be susceptible to an incorrect setting of the over-voltage limit. If incorrectly set (when the pre-charge time constant is over 200 ms), the ESC will prevent motor braking until it receives a zero throttle command. The issue can cause the ESC to get into a state where throttle can only increase, which will almost always result in a crash and can be dangerous for people in the vicinity of the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:98
#: 0739dbaea41b4ebcbf34e99c781d6f1d
msgid "The issue happens due to the following logic in the ESC firmware:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:100
#: 974e5eac6cb24553a9a7fb2caaa32396
msgid "200 ms after ESC startup the supply voltage is sampled, where the maximum voltage is taken as 120% of this point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:101
#: 9d3f5450adc249cda4f296a113e4aed6
msgid "At any time after that, if the supply voltage is above this level, then an over-voltage error is raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:102
#: 0836c2a0139f44358da511e3426674eb
msgid "While an over-voltage error is raised, the throttle will not be reduced unless the autopilot demands a zero throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:104
#: 85e57aad36b34b4984d234fc0da9155e
msgid "This feature aimed to prevent motor braking from pushing too much power back into the batteries, which could lead to overcharging of the batteries or excessive spikes on the ESC inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:107
#: b119fb5e81cc4367a8ec232103f9dab9
msgid "The issue happens if the rise time of the supply voltage is slow enough that the voltage reaches less than 80% of the actual supply voltage within 200 ms. This can happen when using anti-spark connectors to connect the batteries, particularly with long wiring and significant levels of added capacitance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:111
#: e068798cc8c24755a45c4d5b5cc8a84d
msgid "A firmware update, which resolves the above issue, is available and can be found within the links below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:113
#: 8648b173946d4acf83e5d9a146a951f7
msgid "`HV, HV Pro and UHV firmware <https://docs.powerdrives.net/downloads/firmware-releases/uhv-and-hv-pro-firmware#2.1.0-20th-december-2022-latest>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-issues.rst:115
#: 7e08952428374d62bca70f5620d514e9
msgid "`F-Series firmware <https://docs.powerdrives.net/downloads/firmware-releases/f-series-production-firmware>`__."
msgstr ""
